<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{D2D8F612-5A23-5408-6354-6302CEBB3363}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="49" name="Text Placeholder 48"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{9FC067AA-4673-B6C3-F311-10F2E79977CF}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="62"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="327208" y="1932495"/><a:ext cx="11571192" cy="4628642"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr><a:normAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB"/><a:t> </a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="21" name="Text Placeholder 20"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{5D74E217-E0C0-A265-FBC8-CB50CEF8E811}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="33"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="568258" y="2046749"/><a:ext cx="10955148" cy="4298488"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Key details: In August 2024, </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"><a:hlinkClick r:id="rId2"/></a:rPr><a:t>Delta H Innovations</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t> created the Cool&gt;Can, a packaging solution that cools drinks on the go. The packaging looks similar to a regular can but has self-cooling technology infused in it which can be activated upon the pressing of a button. The drink can be cooled down in less then two minutes. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Moreover, the Cool&gt;Can is recyclable and the cooling reactant chamber can also be disposed of in regular garbage bins. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Target audience: This innovation is designed for consumers seeking to enjoy cool beverages without the need for conventional refrigeration, which is often too bulky to carry on the go or inconvenient to fit into small spaces. Cool&gt;Can offers a portable and space-efficient solution, ideal for those who want chilled drinks wherever they are. Moreover, Delta H's </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"><a:hlinkClick r:id="rId3"/></a:rPr><a:t>survey</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t> of students from Nottingham Trent University revealed that 81% of consumers would choose a self-cooling can over a normal can while on the go. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Commercial indicators: The RTD market, which this innovation targets, is predicted to reach $40 billion by 2027. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Now what? Could your brand bring convenience to multiple touchpoints of consumers' everyday lives?</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t>Related Trend(s): Cult of Immediacy</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Number Placeholder 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{0375CFC6-DC4A-67